# The apply worker's credentials. Copy to worker/.env and fill in.
#
# THERE IS NO SERVICE-ROLE KEY HERE, AND THERE CANNOT BE. The backend is Lovable
# Cloud-managed: it injects SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY into edge functions at
# runtime, where it is not retrievable or listable by anyone. That is a better
# arrangement than the one it replaced — the key that can read every candidate's
# private résumé now exists only inside the platform, never in a file.
#
# So the worker holds a credential for the apply-broker edge function instead.
# It grants exactly five operations — claim, release, uncertain, pending, ping —
# and nothing else. If this secret leaks, someone can move application packets
# around. They cannot read a résumé, a mandate, or anyone else's data.

# The deployed broker.
APPLY_BROKER_URL="https://bwhdazbotpblihdxcmho.supabase.co/functions/v1/apply-broker"

# Lovable -> Backend -> Secrets -> APPLY_WORKER_SECRET. Paste the value here.
# Never commit this file; worker/.gitignore already excludes it.
APPLY_WORKER_SECRET=""

# Stop once the queue is dry. 0 keeps the worker polling forever, which is what
# `watch` wants and what a scheduled run does not.
WORKER_IDLE_EXIT_MS="120000"

# Politeness between submissions, and a longer gap before touching the SAME
# employer twice. Employers' forms are not ours to hammer, and the four vendors
# this drives have no bot wall — a courtesy to respect, not an absence to use.
APPLY_GAP_MS="20000"
APPLY_EMPLOYER_GAP_MS="120000"
